{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbF4uzqjzrvVQ1PNUKQp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UCHJq9YeiNE8ALSdFZPmA9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"C=$(./board post candidate '{\"name\": \"Cu (perfect fcc crystal)\", \"family\": \"validation_metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"formula\": \"Cu\", \"rationale\": \"Requested system: defect-free fcc Cu at 300 K, self-diffusion via MD.\"}' --fulfills 58213584-2660-45c1-b7c1-6bbea98a97ec:0); echo \"$C\"\nID=$(echo \"$C\" | grep -oE '[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f-]{27}' | head -1); echo ID=$ID\ncat > /tmp/rr.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\": \"refused\",\n \"task\": \"self_diffusion (cm2/s) of Cu in a perfect fcc Cu crystal at 300 K via molecular dynamics\",\n \"reason\": \"PREMISE CHECK FAILED - the quantity is not measurable with MD as posed. (1) In a perfect (defect-free) crystal there are no vacancies or interstitials, so atoms only vibrate about lattice sites; the MSD reaches a bounded vibrational plateau (~0.01-0.02 A^2 at 300 K) and the long-time slope is zero up to noise/drift. Any D fitted from such a run would be an artifact of thermostat drift, centre-of-mass motion or fit window, not a physical diffusion coefficient. Spontaneous Frenkel-pair formation (several eV) never occurs on ns timescales at 300 K. (2) Even real (vacancy-mediated) Cu self-diffusion at 300 K is astronomically slow: with a literature activation energy of order 2.0-2.2 eV and kT = 0.0259 eV, exp(-Q/kT) ~ 1e-34 to 1e-37, giving D of roughly 1e-34 to 1e-38 cm2/s (order-of-magnitude extrapolation from high-temperature Arrhenius behaviour, not a measured 300 K value). The equilibrium vacancy fraction at 300 K (~exp(-1.2..1.3 eV/kT) ~ 1e-21) means a simulation cell of 1e5-1e6 atoms contains zero thermal vacancies. (3) The smallest D resolvable by MD is ~MSD_resolution/(6t): ~1e-18 cm2 / (6 x 1e-8 s) ~ 1e-11 cm2/s for a 10 ns run, i.e. >20 orders of magnitude above the physical value. Hence no MD run (any engine, any MLIP, any accessible size/length) can measure this; running would produce a spurious number. The calibration file /data/calibration/tier1.json has no diffusion data for Cu to validate against either. WELL-POSED ALTERNATIVES I can run instead: (a) vacancy-mediated self-diffusion of Cu via D = f a^2 nu* exp(-(E_f^v + E_m^v)/kT), computing vacancy formation energy by relaxation and migration barrier by NEB with the MLIP, then evaluating at 300 K (reports a transition-state-theory estimate, validated against experimental high-T Arrhenius Q and the Cu melting point 1357.77 K from tier1.json as a model sanity check); (b) direct MD of D in fcc Cu with an inserted vacancy at high T (e.g. 900-1300 K), fitting an Arrhenius law and reporting Q/D0 (extrapolation to 300 K flagged as such); (c) self-diffusion of liquid Cu just above its melting point (~1400 K), which MD measures directly (~1e-5 cm2/s scale) with block-averaged uncertainty. Please confirm which alternative is wanted.\"}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent $ID"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1476,"cache_read_input_tokens":19512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1476,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74e6e914-0deb-4991-a0f5-7f18d2e79c81","uuid":"68aa2050-cf6d-48ca-9722-464377757979","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:14:52.889Z","request_id":"req_011CgbF4udm5Vib3uPJnNJ7o","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UCHJq9YeiNE8ALSdFZPmA9":{"command":"cd /work && C=$(./board post candidate '{\"name\": \"Cu (perfect fcc crystal)\", \"family\": \"validation_metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"formula\": \"Cu\", \"rationale\": \"Requested system: defect-free fcc 