ier by NEB with the MLIP, then evaluating at 300 K (reports a transition-state-theory estimate, validated against experimental high-T Arrhenius Q and the Cu melting point 1357.77 K from tier1.json as a model sanity check); (b) direct MD of D in fcc Cu with an inserted vacancy at high T (e.g. 900-1300 K), fitting an Arrhenius law and reporting Q/D0 (extrapolation to 300 K flagged as such); (c) self-diffusion of liquid Cu just above its melting point (~1400 K), which MD measures directly (~1e-5 cm2/s scale) with block-averaged uncertainty. Please confirm which alternative is wanted.\"}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent $ID"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01UCHJq9YeiNE8ALSdFZPmA9":{"cwd":"/work"}}}
